s incorporated in 1997 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joel D. Becker | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 216 people. Revenue per employee of $463K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $51K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Neuropace, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $310M market cap on $100M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +30% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -201% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 74% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $11M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 16.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 313% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"NeuroPace (NPCE) Securities Investigation Notice - Levi & Korsinsky","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/neuropace-npce-securities-investigation-notice---levi--korsinsky-302947293.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795446060.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"NPCE Investors Have Opportunity to Join NeuroPace, Inc. Fraud Investigation with SBS Law","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/npce-investors-have-opportunity-to-join-neuropace-inc-fraud-investigation-with-sbs-law-302947792.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795408620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"How Neuropace Inc. (NPCE) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.st